Sales onboarding – Day 5 – Who is our competition?

Please take your time for your self-research regarding our primary competitors. Marketing has prepared an overview of our competitors [in this presentation](https://kontentai.sharepoint.com/:b:/s/ExecutiveTeam-Teams/Ea%5Fm3baYXxtFjH8Lx5QRfoEB1Uz1YbZ8RewvVYTlBa5CXg?e=245dAn) (obsolete). ;

On top of that, we can share this [Public Competitor Content](https://kontent-ai.atlassian.net/wiki/x/moIR) that could help as well. ;

Or we can compete in the [security aspect](http://Competitive Comparison of Compliance and Security Certifications) as well. ;

When you select Kontent.ai as your new headless CMS, there are many questions you may have:

* How do you integrate Kontent.ai with your existing toolset that works well for you?
* What about your existing content and technology infrastructure? ;
* Can you widen the range of tools for your operations after you move to Kontent.ai? ;

The translation process begins and is triggered in Kontent.ai. You react to the trigger by creating a translation unit tailor-made for the translation management system (TMS). The translation unit might contain one or more content items that need to be translated.

Once the translation unit is processed on the TMS's side, you get a new translation unit back. Now you import the translated content from the new translation unit to your Kontent.ai project.

In the following lessons, you'll learn what decisions you need to make to create translation units with the right content an integration with the TMS that works ;

To make things clear in your onboarding. You will work with these apps: ;

* **Asana** — where is your main onboarding programme, which is separated into four main sections to keep your tasks organized and grouped. Each section follows a single week (5 days of your onboarding)
* **Confluence by JIRA** — the "corporate Wikipedia" where all the knowledge is stored; imagine different Spaces, many pages, and processes listed there. It is our knowledge hub with all the information scattered across the whole app, as many other teams or individuals use Confluence. ;
* **Kontent.ai Learn Portal** — which is an in-house developed Learning Management System, for the training purposes of our customers and not only them. As we need to keep track of your onboarding progress and test your knowledge, our Learn portal is the perfect tool for that. ;

So now, get ready to dive into the Kontent.ai Learning portal! This dynamic platform sources its **content straight from Kontent.ai**, opening up a world of possibilities for you to contribute. From the get-go, you're invited to collaborate and become an integral part of the Kontent.ai team. Let's get started!

Please follow and bookmark the delegated [**Sales Onboarding Project in Asana**](https://app.asana.com/1/1204058094034299/project/1206170083809775/board/1208027485165651) created for you, which will guide you through the first month. On top of this Project, there is a second one that is connected to the **General HR Onboarding** project, which will drive any other operational tasks. ;

**Ensure to read through the agenda and focus on daily tasks.** Moreover, the sessions with other team leaders and departments will be scheduled and added to your calendar later. Eventually, you will create the first meetings based on the Tasks in your onboarding project in Asana. ;

The Enablement team will manage and oversee the first two weeks of scheduling. Then, you are expected to manage the rest of the scheduling based on your needs. Additionally, your team or team leader will forward meetings so you have access to regular weekly/monthly team/company sessions. ;

_To sum it up, it is expected that you will always have your Asana tasks up to date, follow the due dates, and work on your activities in this Learn portal as you progress through your onboarding day by day. ;_

The onboarding supervisor and buddy will work closely with you from the beginning to shape the program and invite you to real meetings/sessions very soon. Be prepared! 😎

Lastly, please let your supervisor and onboarding buddy know if you find any broken links or inaccurate, obsolete, or misleading resources. Together, we can improve the resources even more!

**The expected agenda is as follows: ;**

* 1st week — getting to know everybody at Kontent.ai and understanding the onboarding structure and internal processes
* 2nd week — get Product knowledge, be familiar with the tasks and the next steps, and understand the way of working within the closest team
* 3rd week — get Sales knowledge and be able to work on the next steps and plan your calendar accordingly to your tasks
* 4th week — do Shadowing and practicing, and be able to train yourself on the provided resources with the help of others; self-sufficiency in some areas is expected already

Since Kontent.ai is an ever-changing company with many processes being updated regularly, please expect an agile approach and changes along the way. If in doubt, always reach out to your leader, who provides additional guidance and help. Communication is the key! ;

Got some feedback? Don't hold back! Your input can help refine and elevate the overall experience, benefiting you and new team members.

Thank you, and once again: "Welcome to Kontent.ai. We are happy to have you!" ;

